From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shupeng Xue <dspxue@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 13:09:32 +1100
Subject: [PATCH wireless-next 05/11] wifi: b43: HT-PHY: read the low half of
 32-bit table entries first

Reading the DATALO register latches the high half of a 32-bit table
entry into DATAHI; reading DATAHI first returns whatever the previous
table access left there. N-PHY and brcmsmac read the low half first,
HT-PHY did it the other way round.

The only 32-bit read is in b43_phy_ht_tx_power_fix(), which runs on
every channel switch and copies the high half of a TX gain table entry
into the per-core TX gain table. That got a stale value.

Fixes: 1a9313923718 ("b43: HT-PHY: prepare place for HT-PHY tables")
Assisted-by: pi:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/tables_phy_ht.c | 13 +++++++------
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/tables_phy_ht.c b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/tables_phy_ht.c
index 1acf2df66e5e..3b91bfffb09e 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/tables_phy_ht.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/tables_phy_ht.c
@@ -621,10 +621,10 @@ u32 b43_httab_read(struct b43_wldev *dev, u32 offset)
 		value = b43_phy_read(dev, B43_PHY_HT_TABLE_DATALO);
 		break;
 	case B43_HTTAB_32BIT:
+		/* Low half first: reading DATALO latches the high half */
 		b43_phy_write(dev, B43_PHY_HT_TABLE_ADDR, offset);
-		value = b43_phy_read(dev, B43_PHY_HT_TABLE_DATAHI);
-		value <<= 16;
-		value |= b43_phy_read(dev, B43_PHY_HT_TABLE_DATALO);
+		value = b43_phy_read(dev, B43_PHY_HT_TABLE_DATALO);
+		value |= b43_phy_read(dev, B43_PHY_HT_TABLE_DATAHI) << 16;
 		break;
 	default:
 		B43_WARN_ON(1);
@@ -658,9 +658,10 @@ void b43_httab_read_bulk(struct b43_wldev *dev, u32 offset,
 			data += 2;
 			break;
 		case B43_HTTAB_32BIT:
-			*((u32 *)data) = b43_phy_read(dev, B43_PHY_HT_TABLE_DATAHI);
-			*((u32 *)data) <<= 16;
-			*((u32 *)data) |= b43_phy_read(dev, B43_PHY_HT_TABLE_DATALO);
+			*((u32 *)data) =
+				b43_phy_read(dev, B43_PHY_HT_TABLE_DATALO);
+			*((u32 *)data) |=
+				b43_phy_read(dev, B43_PHY_HT_TABLE_DATAHI) << 16;
 			data += 4;
 			break;
 		default:
